@notice Storage-layout and upgrade-safety checks by OpenZeppelin's validator (`@openzeppelin/upgrades-core`).
 @dev Runs `npx` through FFI, so it needs Node.js and network access the first time. It checks what plain tests
      cannot: ERC-7201 namespaces not colliding or shrinking, no constructor / selfdestruct / delegatecall misuse,
      and that each V2 is layout-compatible with its V1 ("oz-upgrades-from" annotation on each mock).
      The validator reads build-info files and fails on stale ones from earlier builds, so these tests only run
      when VALIDATE_UPGRADES=true, through `make check-upgrades` which does `forge clean` first (CI runs it too).
